  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nA midlevel trof will dig into the Great Lakes and interior NE CONUS\nthis evening into tonight, with an attendant cold front sweeping\nthrough the OH Vly during this time. This FROPA will provide a\nreinforcement of seasonably cool and dry air, which will settle in\nthrough the first part of the upcoming workweek. \n\nThe main item of interest through the next few days will be the\npotential for some patchy frost to develop, especially in\nrural/sheltered spots, for Monday night. The center of sfc high \npressure will be drifting just east of the ILN FA toward 12z Tuesday,\nwith clear skies and calm winds creating favorable conditions for\nsome patchy frost to develop. This will primarily be a concern in\nsheltered/low-lying areas and for spots near/north of I-70, with\nprobs for minimum temps at/below 38F between 20-30% by daybreak\nTuesday in these areas. Adjusted overnight temps toward NBM 25th\npercentile to account for this setup. These temps, alongside ideal \nradiational cooling conditions, pose a scenario where some patchy \nfrost will be possible in an isolated capacity. There isn't quite \nenough confidence in the coverage or potential for frost to add to \nthe official fcst or even the HWO, but it is mentioned here for \ngeneral awareness. Some patchy frost cannot be ruled out again \nTuesday night into Wednesday, primarily for low- lying/sheltered \nareas of central/south-central OH and NE KY. \n\nAfter daytime highs in the lower to mid 70s today, below normal temps\nare favored both Monday and Tuesday as highs reach into the mid to\nupper 60s. Warmer air will slowly build back into the OH Vly midweek\nand beyond, with highs reaching into the upper 70s to lower 80s by\nWednesday through the remainder of the workweek. \n\nKey Message 2) \n\nBy next weekend, a developing low initially over the Gulf and TX \nwill progress to the N/NE into the OH/TN Vlys, bringing widespread \nrain chances back into the region by late Saturday into Sunday. This \nwill be the next appreciable chance for rain locally, with mainly dry\nconditions favored until then.",
